  "behavior": {
    "sourceSelection": "Known sources use Metadata API 1.17. ESKA selects the full retained query owner, then the explicitly supplied dirty native buffer, then disk. The adapter verifies binary chunk offsets, canonical base64 and the full SHA-256, and closes all temporary handles.",
    "adapter": "eska-protected no longer reads file content through workspace.fs. Its Native provider implements URI translation, readonly capability, presentation stat times/sizes, event routing and bounded readonly retry. Native directory metadata/listing remain IDE presentation operations. There is no persistent source-body cache or new backend process per view.",
    "unclassifiedPreview": "Opt-in API 1.18 source/previewOpen/Read/Close serves disk-only snapshots below the process working directory captured at startup. It works after initialize even if the manifest is absent or invalid. Traversal, absolute paths, directories and aliases escaping the canonical root are rejected. Protection is unknown/unclassified and always writable:false; a preview grants no metadata, source-session or write authority.",
    "authority": "Metadata and unclassified view handles cannot read/close each other. Workspace close drops handles without recycling connection IDs; EOF/shutdown frees all state. The existing 16-view, 32 MiB and 64-entry budgets remain shared with query documents/sessions/uploads.",
    "retainedOwner": "An active source session outranks a newer ordinary native buffer. The installed provider shows its exact full dirty parent; stat size matches that body. Session release refreshes the view to the current native buffer/disk and does not save the owner or prolong the source lease.",
    "supportEvents": "Parsed rule bytes and the acknowledged filesystem-event fingerprint are separate. A source read cannot consume a pending rule change. An acknowledged repeated event with unchanged bytes retains the existing no-rebuild optimization.",
    "virtualEvents": "Physical source, manifest, analyzer-config, shallow-directory and provider mirror watchers check URI scheme. Virtual events with the same fsPath cannot become workspace/didChangeFiles notifications, trigger metadata feedback or restart the owned LSP.",
    "compatibility": "The same-process 1.17 fallback retains ordinary source snapshots and native write protection. Metadata-independent previews require 1.18. Durable XML sessions retain their 1.16 contract.",
    "nativeBoundary": "Readonly provider acceptance does not prove a freeze of every ordinary file: BSL tab or preservation/restoration of a native session override. Source application for BSL remains disabled; the earlier strict native-lock findings are unchanged.",
    "backendWritesOwner": false,
    "newDependencies": false
  },
